 "integration": {
  "summary": "On the controller set LAN 1 to Modbus TCP/IP, turn on Modbus communication, write access and extended monitor data, then poll the controller at port 502, unit ID 255. To make it fire, write 1 to holding 402, the flow setpoint (°C) to 400 and 7 to the strategy bit block 405; read outdoor 0, system flow 4, boiler 1 flow 8001 and status 8012/8013.",
  "minimum_registers": [
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 402,
    "why": "Heat generator operating mode (on/off)"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 400,
    "why": "System flow temperature setpoint"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 405,
    "why": "Strategy bit block (temperature- or output-led)"
   },
   {
    "table": "holding_register",
    "address": 0,
    "why": "Heartbeat counter"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 0,
    "why": "Outdoor temperature"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 4,
    "why": "System flow temperature"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 5,
    "why": "System HMI status"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 8001,
    "why": "Boiler 1 flow temperature"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 8013,
    "why": "Boiler 1 status bits (burner on, faults)"
   },
   {
    "table": "input_register",
    "address": 476,
    "why": "Fault register 1 (message key)"
   }
  ],
  "enable": "Service menu > Connectivity: Local Area Network = Modbus TCP/IP (factory: Internet); Modbus communication = with or without heartbeat ('No' disables Modbus); Allow write access = On; Provide extended monitor data = On (factory Off, required for Modbus data). Then Service menu > Heat generation > Strategy data > Basic settings: enable 'Heat demand via Modbus' (and disable 'Internal heat demand' for exclusive BMS control).",
  "watchdog": "With 'Modbus communication = with heartbeat', the BMS must keep writing a changing counter to holding 0; holding 1 echoes it. If no new value arrives within the timeout (120-600 s, default 180 s) the controller raises a 'connection to building management faulty' message. 'Without heartbeat' disables loss detection.",
  "quirks": [
   "Addresses in the list are already 0-based wire addresses; add 30001/40001 only if your BMS uses Modicon notation.",
   "32-bit values (starts, operating time, fault keys) are high word first; some BMSs read the unsigned fault keys as negative signed values.",
   "The display code at 8019 is two ASCII characters packed into one register.",
   "Temperature demand (400) is whole degrees while most temperatures read back are x10."
  ],
  "setup": [
   "Connect LAN 1 on the BCT 531 module to the BMS network; do not use the 172.31.42.x range, which the controller uses internally.",
   "Set a static IP (or DHCP) in the Connectivity menu and save.",
   "The unit ID is 255 by default; the guide says it can be changed from firmware 1.5.13 (the download page says 1.6).",
   "Firmware below 1.3 uses an older address list; a compatibility mode for firmware below 1.3.6 exists but should only be enabled for existing old integrations."
  ],
  "gotchas": [
   "The strategy bit block must include the lead-boiler bit (bit 0) from firmware 1.3.3, and with an FM-CM cascade module the lead-boiler function must be enabled.",
   "Output-led demand (401) works only in exclusive mode (internal heat demand off) and only when all boilers on the controller are the same type.",
   "Points for hardware that is not fitted still answer, with invalid values such as 0 °C; writes to them are accepted but have no effect.",
   "A boiler in lockout or manual mode ignores heat demand until it is ready again."
  ]
 },
